npm db:gen" "DATABASE_URL=<macOS-keychain:etzhayyim.rw/ROOT_URL> pnpm db:drift" "uv run python -m compileall graph_schema alembic"] :manual_remaining_files [] :runtime_env_revisions ["30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/versions/r_0003_iceberg_sinks.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/versions/r_20260421170000_udf_external_python_fix_and_classify_t3.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/versions/r_20260424170000_news_intel_udf.py"] :hummock_only_default true :optional_iceberg_sinks "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/versions/r_0003_iceberg_sinks.py is a no-op unless ENABLE_ICEBERG_SINKS=true; Nessie/S3 env vars are not required for the current Hummock-only path."}} :knowledge {:hf-dataset-quality-catalog-20260509 {:discovered_on "2026-05-09" :category "graph-schema" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Hugging Face dataset trust, curated lists, and top-quality candidates are managed as Kotoba/Datomic graph state" :details "`r_20260509210000_hf_dataset_quality_catalog` adds the Kotoba/Datomic graph layer\nfor Hugging Face dataset governance:\n- vertex_hf_dataset_collection\n- vertex_hf_dataset_reliability\n- edge_hf_dataset_collection_member\n- edge_hf_dataset_reliability_about\n- mv_hf_dataset_quality_top\n\nThe migration also creates lookup indexes for collection id, dataset repo,\nmodality, decision, and edge src/dst scans.\n\nSeed collection `multimodal-poc-curated-v1` contains 17 curated reliability\nrecords and 17 member/about edges. Verified MV top candidates include\n`openslr/librispeech_asr`, `google/fleurs`,\n`BIFOLD-BigEarthNetv2-0/BigEarthNet.txt`, `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu`, and\n`ds4sd/DocLayNet`.\n\nPayload ingestion is separate from dataset governance. As of this entry,\n`Roman1111111/claude-opus-4.6-10000x` is active with 9633 ingested records, and\n`angrygiraffe/claude-opus-4.6-4.7-reasoning-8.7k` is active with 8706 canonical\n`full_train.jsonl` records.\n\nDDL should be applied only after `70-tools/scripts/ingest/rw-health-gate.sh`.\nDuring the 2026-05-09 incident window, foreground MV creation was blocked by\ncluster-wide barrier / Hummock version lag; the final MV was created with\n`SET BACKGROUND_DDL = true` after Kotoba/Datomic recovered.\n" :impact "HF dataset selection, multimodal training data governance, Kotoba/Datomic vertex/edge/MV catalog operations" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260509210000_hf_dataset_quality_catalog.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509210000_hf_dataset_quality_catalog.up.sql" "30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509210000_hf_dataset_quality_catalog.down.sql" "70-tools/scripts/ingest/hf-dataset-quality-seed.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/src/database.ts"]} :bigquery-public-data-ingest-cost-topology-20260509 {:discovered_on "2026-05-09" :category "graph-schema" :severity "info" :status "proposed" :summary "BigQuery public datasets are P0 catalog/sample and P1 profiling inputs before any Kotoba/Datomic graph projection; international-public-record substrate covering ~17 dim_world_domain app_hosts (patent / blockchain / weather / iryo / maps / US-gov / etc.). JP-vertical and industrial-IoT domains stay on dedicated collectors." :details "ADR-2605092700 defines the public-data ingest split:\n\n- Use BigQuery for public dataset discovery, schema sampling, projection,\n  dedupe, entity matching, time-window aggregation, and training corpus\n  sampling.\n- Use self-ingest for official APIs/files, live updates, WARC/WET/PBF/blob\n  extraction, OCR, and source-specific canonicalization.\n- Store only canonical `vertex_*`, typed `edge_*`, bounded `mv_*`, indexes,\n  and lineage rows in Kotoba/Datomic. Raw/public all-history payloads stay in\n  object storage with `vertex_ingest_artifact` references.\n\nInitial scope is P0 + P1 only. P0 catalogs and samples public dataset metadata.\nP1 profiles selected candidates for keys, null rates, text/language\ndistribution, PII/training risk, license decision, and recommended\nKotoba/Datomic vertex/edge targets. P2 production graph projection is blocked until\nP0/P1 review creates an explicit allowlist and schema plan.\n\nCost model captured in the ADR:\n- on-demand query scan: first 1 TiB/month free, then about USD 6.25/TiB.\n- active logical BigQuery storage: about USD 23.552/TiB-month.\n- P0 catalog/sample (~10 TiB scanned) is about USD 56 one-pass query cost.\n- P1 profiling defaults to 20 TiB/month (about USD 119) with a 100 TiB hard\n  cap (about USD 619) unless explicitly approved.\n- P2 broad projection (~1 PiB scanned) is about USD 6.4k one-pass query cost.\n- Literal all-public-data/all-column copying is rejected; 100 PiB+ scans would\n  be about USD 639k+ before storage, egress, Kotoba/Datomic scale-up, embeddings,\n  OCR, or training GPU.\n\nPlanned graph additions:\n- vertex_public_dataset_catalog\n- vertex_public_dataset_table\n- vertex_public_dataset_sample\n- vertex_public_dataset_profile\n- vertex_bigquery_ingest_job\n- vertex_bigquery_export_artifact\n- vertex_bigquery_profile_run\n- edge_dataset_produces_vertex_type\n- edge_dataset_allowed_for_training_task\n- mv_public_dataset_ingest_status\n- mv_public_dataset_catalog_coverage\n- mv_public_dataset_profile_rank\n- mv_training_source_eligibility\n\nEvery BigQuery-backed ingest must use dry-run/query validation,\n`maximum_bytes_billed`, explicit column lists, partition filters where\navailable, TTL'd staging tables, and `allowed_for_train=false` until license and\nPII policy gates pass.\n\nworld-coverage mapping (formerly driven by `etzhayyim world-coverage`, CLI removed 2026-05-20; 2026-05-10 review):\n\n- BigQuery public-data covers ~17 `dim_world_domain` app_hosts: `patent`,\n  `blockchain`, `weather`, `iryo` (subset), `iryo-genomics`, `maps`, `gov` (US\n  federal), `talent` (US), `bank` (US/FDIC), `finance` (US partial), `shizen`,\n  `tentai`, `text-corpus`, `code`/`package-metadata`, `kuruma-transport` (US),\n  `civic` (US cities), `vision`. Estimated post-P2 coverage delta:\n  `mv_world_coverage_live` from 0.0087% → ~0.05–0.10% (5–10× jump from\n  `patent` / `blockchain` / `weather` / `iryo-genomics` / US `gov` saturating\n  their world totals).\n- BigQuery cannot fill: `photos` (5T), `kessai`/`serial`/`seizo`/`nimotsu`/\n  `bim`/`mac`/`iot` (each 100B–1T, industrial telemetry), `invoice`/`receipt`\n  (each 500B, private), `natural-person` (108B), `shisan`/`haikibutsu`/\n  `kachiku`/`phonenumber`/`keiyaku`/`software` (each 10–50B), all\n  JP-vertical (`anime`/`manga`/`gameya`/`mercari`/`rakuten`/`ndl_books`/\n  `houbun_jp`). These keep their dedicated collector / partnership pipelines.\n- Topology decision: BigQuery is the international-public-record substrate;\n  JP-vertical, industrial-IoT, private-transaction, and PII-observation\n  domains stay on dedicated collectors. The two paths converge at\n  `vertex_*`/`edge_*` in Kotoba/Datomic, never at the BigQuery layer.\n\nP0 surface (landed 2026-05-09):\n- migration `30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509600000_vertex_public_dataset_catalog.{up,down}.sql`\n  + alembic revision `r_20260509600000_vertex_public_dataset_catalog` provisions\n  `vertex_public_dataset_catalog`, `vertex_public_dataset_table`,\n  `vertex_public_dataset_sample`, `vertex_bigquery_ingest_job`,\n  `vertex_bigquery_export_artifact`, `vertex_bigquery_profile_run`, and\n  `mv_public_dataset_catalog_coverage`.\n- runner `70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-catalog.mjs` enforces\n  metadata-first discovery (INFORMATION_SCHEMA), bounded sample queries with\n  `maximumBytesBilled`, artifact persistence to local fs (or `--artifact-prefix`\n  object-store URI), and double-entry write to the BigQuery ledger plus the\n  generic `vertex_ingest_run` / `vertex_ingest_artifact` spine.\n\nP2 adapter pattern (landed 2026-05-11):\n\n- 10 new target vertex tables in migration `20260511000000_p2_bq_target_vertices`\n  (`vertex_air_quality_observation` / `vertex_taxi_trip` / `vertex_qa_post` /\n  `vertex_marine_observation` / `vertex_synthetic_patient` /\n  `vertex_forest_inventory` / `vertex_target_evidence` /\n  `vertex_chemistry_patent` / `vertex_blockchain_block` / `vertex_blockchain_tx`).\n- 11 per-dataset adapters under `70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/` sharing\n  `_lib.mjs` (resumable cursors via `vertex_ingest_cursor`; periodic FLUSH\n  every 20 chunks; `onChunkFlush` mid-run cursor advance; fresh\n  `pg.Client` per record / maintained client per INSERT loop).\n- Bindings gate: `edge_dataset_produces_vertex_type` 13 rows /\n  `edge_dataset_allowed_for_training_task` 44 rows; ADR-2605101000 §D3\n  refuses to dispatch an adapter without its binding.\n- Pilot state (2026-05-11): vertex_air_quality_observation 110,421 +\n  vertex_blockchain_block (ltc) 612 + vertex_blockchain_tx (ltc) 149,543.\n  Cumulative BQ scan P0+P1+P2 = 7.9 TiB ≈ $48.27.\n\nP1 surface (landed 2026-05-09):\n- migration `30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509610000_vertex_public_dataset_profile.{up,down}.sql`\n  + alembic revision `r_20260509610000_vertex_public_dataset_profile` provisions\n  `vertex_public_dataset_profile`, `edge_public_dataset_profiles_table`,\n  `edge_public_dataset_candidate_for_vertex_type`,\n  `edge_public_dataset_candidate_for_training_task`,\n  `edge_dataset_produces_vertex_type`, `edge_dataset_allowed_for_training_task`,\n  `mv_public_dataset_profile_rank`, `mv_training_source_eligibility`, and\n  `mv_public_dataset_ingest_status`.\n- runner `70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-profile.mjs` only operates\n  on P0 candidates whose catalog `review_status <> 'rejected'`, enforces\n  `maximumBytesBilled <= 2 TiB` per query, defaults monthly budget to 20 TiB\n  (100 TiB hard cap requires `--approval-note`), uses `TABLESAMPLE SYSTEM`\n  when the table exceeds the per-query cap, and defaults `allowed_for_train`\n  to `false` until a license + PII review explicitly promotes a row.\n" :impact "public dataset ingest, Kotoba/Datomic graph schema planning, LLM training corpus governance, BigQuery cost controls" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605092700-bigquery-public-data-ingest-cost-topology.md" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260425160000_vertex_ingest_spine.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509600000_vertex_public_dataset_catalog.up.sql" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260509600000_vertex_public_dataset_catalog.py" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-catalog.mjs" "30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509610000_vertex_public_dataset_profile.up.sql" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260509610000_vertex_public_dataset_profile.py" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-profile.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-license-enrich.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-review-update.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-allowlist-export.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-partitioning-review.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/bigquery-public-dataset-bindings-apply.mjs" "30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260511000000_p2_bq_target_vertices.up.sql" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260511000000_p2_bq_target_vertices.py" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/_lib.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/epa-historical-air-quality.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/crypto-litecoin.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/crypto-dogecoin.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/stackoverflow.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/noaa-icoads.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/cms-synthetic-omop.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/usfs-fia.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/open-targets-platform.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/ebi-surechembl.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/new-york-taxi-trips.mjs" "70-tools/scripts/projection/bigquery/chicago-taxi-trips.mjs" "00-contracts/catalogs/bigquery/public-dataset-licenses.json" "90-docs/adr/2605101000-bigquery-p2-projection-design.md" "90-docs/adr/2605070700-rw-native-model-training-weight-lineage.md"]} :generic-decision-context-graph-20260509 {:discovered_on "2026-05-09" :category "graph-schema" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Generic capability / constraint / dependency context graph for agent loops, conversations, processes, and infrastructure" :details "`20260509170000_context_capability_constraint_dependency.ts` adds the generic\ndecision-context substrate:\n- vertex_context_subject\n- vertex_context_capability\n- vertex_context_constraint\n- vertex_context_dependency\n- edge_context_has_capability\n- edge_context_constrained_by\n- edge_context_depends_on\n\nThe schema is intentionally not infra-specific. `subject_ref` can identify an\nagent loop, conversation, process, training action, app, ADR, infra component,\nor arbitrary decision subject. Direction contract:\n- edge_context_depends_on.src_vid depends on edge_context_depends_on.dst_vid\n- edge_context_constrained_by.src_vid is constrained by dst_vid\n- edge_context_has_capability.src_vid has capability dst_vid\n\nLive apply note: Kotoba/Datomic recovered repeatedly during this session and\nforeground view / FLUSH paths returned meta-service recovery errors. To avoid\nreintroducing heavy DDL, the migration now keeps only base vertex/edge tables\nand lightweight lookup indexes. MCP reads base tables directly and falls back\nfrom `mv_context_decision_surface` if a future view is absent.\n\nOka seed rows are live:\n- subject=3 (`oka-training`, `oka-training:a40-fp8`, `oka-training:l40s-fp8`)\n- capability=2 (A40 BF16 fallback, L40S FP8 training)\n- constraint=2 (A40 FP8 hard block, FP8 BF16/FP32 fallback requirement)\n- dependency=1 (L40S FP8 capacity + implementation gate)\n- edges: has_capability=2, constrained_by=2, depends_on=1\n\nOka H100/27B session closeout is recorded in the top-level `deps.toml` and\nADR-2605092345: HF quality ingest added 4,900 records; Unsloth Gemma 3 27B\nLoRA SFT completed 100 steps with `train_loss=1.297047061920166`; inference\neval measured base 5.0904 tok/s vs adapter 4.9798 tok/s; the public HF adapter\nrepo is `com-junkawasaki/oka-gemma3-27b-hf-quality-lora` at commit\n`8ef48c441d0342ec3d6f04c2f955be95b0866dbb`; and the temporary RunPod H100 NVL\npod `etzhayyim-h100nvl-train-260509` was terminated after artifact preservation.\n" :impact "agent decision memory, process routing, training precision policy, MCP context retrieval" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260509170000_context_capability_constraint_dependency.ts" "50-infra/cloudflare/workers/atproto/src/mcp-adapter.ts" "90-docs/adr/2605092345-runpod-l40s-fp8-multimodal-model-design.md"]} :capability-projection-ssot-20260413 {:discovered_on "2026-04-13" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "resolved" :summary "Kotoba/Datomic graph is capability declaration/projection SSoT, not contract SSoT" :details "Capability contract remains in Lexicon.\nKotoba/Datomic stores normalized query state: actor, capability, policy, permission-set, and their relationships.\nRecommended projection shape:\n- vertex_actor\n- vertex_capability\n- vertex_policy\n- edge_actor_has_capability\n- edge_actor_bound_role\n- edge_capability_requires_permission\n- edge_capability_calls_capability\nJSON-LD stays as declaration source, but operational reads should target projected vertex/edge tables.\n" :impact "graph schema design, policy query layer, actor discovery"} :rw-capability-storage-authority-20260509 {:discovered_on "2026-05-09" :category "security-architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Kotoba/Datomic stores capability hashes/grants/authority projections, not bearer caps or protected plaintext" :details "ADR-2605092700 accepts RW capability storage and authority boundary:\n\n- RW remains the queryable graph/materialized-view plane.\n- RW may store cap_hash, verify indexes, grant facts, delegation chains,\n  caveats, revocation state, encrypted manifests, and audit rows.\n- RW must not store raw read/write/admin capability secrets, DEKs, or protected\n  plaintext for migrated object classes.\n- auth.etzhayyim.com remains the OAuth/DPoP proof-of-possession session boundary.\n- Capability evaluation normalizes did:web / did:plc facade DIDs to canonical\n  `did:erc725:etzhayyim:260425:<identity>` root DIDs before grant matching.\n- ERC725 / ERC-8004 remain the trust/discovery anchors; RW is the operational\n  projection and verification index, not a replacement for the onchain root\n  identity registry.\n\nTarget logical relations:\n- vertex_cap_object\n- vertex_cap_grant\n- edge_cap_delegates\n- vertex_cap_revocation\n- vertex_cap_audit\n\nTarget MVs:\n- mv_cap_effective_grant\n- mv_cap_subject_authority\n- mv_cap_object_visibility\n- mv_cap_revocation_closure\n" :impact "RW protected-object schema, MCP capability verifier, auth.etzhayyim.com integration, ERC725 root DID authority" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605092700-rw-capability-storage-authority.md" "90-docs/260424-oauth-strict-mode-cutover-runbook.md" "90-docs/adr/2604262100-erc725-erc8004-k8s-ipfs-agent-runtime.md" "50-infra/vultr/geth-private/contracts/ADDRESSES.md"]} :llm-camunda-zeebe-license-policy-rag-20260429 {:discovered_on "2026-04-29" :category "software-compliance" :severity "warning" :status "superseded" :summary "Superseded Camunda/Zeebe 8.5 compatibility RAG seed" :details "`20260429161000_seed_camunda_zeebe_license_policy.ts` seeds\n`vertex_domain_knowledge_document`, source records, chunks, and citation edges\nfor the earlier Camunda/Zeebe licensing decision. The retrievable policy says:\npin the broker to `camunda/zeebe:8.5.23` for the short-term Zeebe-only\ncompatibility track, do not add Operate / Tasklist / Optimize /\nElasticsearch / OpenSearch dependencies without license review, and do not move\nback to Camunda 8.6+ self-managed production without Enterprise/SaaS approval\nor an approved replacement.\n\nThe seed also records that 8.5 is EOL and that the live downgrade from 8.6.39\nmust be treated as fresh broker state unless an explicit compatibility review\nproves otherwise.\n\nSuperseded operationally on 2026-04-30: live Zeebe remains\n`camunda/zeebe:8.6.39` in Zeebe-only mode without Operate / Tasklist /\nOptimize / Elasticsearch / OpenSearch. Prefer `deps.toml`\n`zeebe-86-zeebe-only-runtime-20260430` and `50-infra/vultr/zeebe/zeebe.yaml`\nfor current operations.\n" :impact "LLM policy retrieval, software compliance answers, Zeebe runtime guardrails" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260429161000_seed_camunda_zeebe_license_policy.ts" "90-docs/adr/0056-bpmn-as-actor.md" "50-infra/vultr/zeebe/8.5-downgrade-runbook.md"]} :curpus2skill-corpus-skill-evidence-schema-20260430 {:discovered_on "2026-04-30" :category "graph-schema" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "curpus2skill evidence tables link corpus documents to existing vertex_skill rows" :details "`20260430400000_corpus_skill_extraction.ts` adds\n`vertex_corpus_skill_extraction_run` and `edge_corpus_skill_evidence`.\nThe extractor is evidence-only: it records matched corpus snippets,\nscore/match kind, source table, source actor DID, and extraction run metadata.\nIt intentionally does not create or mutate `vertex_skill`.\n\n`20260430401000_seed_curpus2skill_bpmn.ts` seeds the BPMN process definition\nfor `curpus2skill_extract_evidence`, which is deployed to Zeebe by the existing\nBPMN watcher.\n" :impact "skill graph evidence, legal corpus enrichment, BPMN extraction runs" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260430400000_corpus_skill_extraction.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260430401000_seed_curpus2skill_bpmn.ts" "00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/curpus2skill/extractEvidence.bpmn" "70-tools/scripts/curpus2skill.mjs"]} :pd-color-process-mining-views-20260429 {:discovered_on "2026-04-29" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PD color process mining exports are canonical DB views, not committed CSV snapshots" :details "`20260429161000_pd_color_process_mining_views.ts` creates\n`view_pd_color_process_event_log` and `view_pd_color_process_case_summary`.\nThe event log view unions fine-grained `vertex_pd_color_process_event` rows\nfrom Zeebe worker tasks with coarser run, rights, derivative, localization, and\npublication graph records.\n\nDo not reintroduce committed `pdcolor-event-log.csv` or\n`pdcolor-process-summary.json` snapshots. Export on demand from the Python actor\nimage via `python -m kotodama.pd_color_process_mining csv|summary`.\n" :impact "process mining, PM4Py/Celonis export, PD color graph analytics" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260429161000_pd_color_process_mining_views.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/src/database.ts" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/pd_color_process_mining.py" "60-apps/etzhayyim-project-public-domain-colorization/process-mining/README.md"]} :canonical-process-mining-rw-udf-20260429 {:discovered_on "2026-04-29" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Kotoba/Datomic canonical process mining function is bpmn_analyze_process" :details "Generic process mining is exposed from Kotoba/Datomic as\n`bpmn_analyze_process(VARCHAR)`, created by\n`20260429193000_udf_bpmn_analyze_process.ts`. The function delegates to the\nshared mitama UDF pool under NSID `com.etzhayyim.apps.bpmn.analyzeProcess`.\n\nInputs are a JSON object with optional `processId`, `caseId`, `actionPrefix`,\n`since`, `until`, `limit`, and `includeLlm`. Outputs are JSON with\n`eventCount`, `caseCount`, `activityCount`, `activities`, `bottlenecks`,\n`variants`, `cases`, `anomalies`, and optional `llm` diagnosis. Treat this as\nthe default DB-side process mining primitive; do not route generic requests to\nCamunda Optimize.\n" :impact "Kotoba/Datomic analytics, XRPC UDF routing, process mining defaults" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260429193000_udf_bpmn_analyze_process.ts" "00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/bpmn/analyzeProcess.json" "50-infra/cloudflare/workers/atproto/src/handlers/etzhayyim/udf-pool.ts" "90-docs/adr/0056-bpmn-as-actor.md"]} :graph-sos-intel-actor-schema-20260507 {:discovered_on "2026-05-07" :category "graph-schema" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Graph SoS Intel actor persists compact topology snapshots and findings" :details "`20260507170000_graph_sos_intel.ts` creates the minimal Kotoba/Datomic graph tables\nfor the T1 Graph SoS Intel actor: snapshots, findings, finding-to-relation\nedges, and relation inventory observations. The actor reads\n`information_schema.tables` and `pg_indexes` directly during ticks, but the\ninitial migration deliberately avoids `CREATE INDEX` and catalog `CREATE VIEW`\nbecause those DDL forms stalled or failed against the live Kotoba/Datomic meta\nservice during 2026-05-07 application.\n" :impact "graph topology intelligence, actor audit rows, Kotoba/Datomic DDL safety" :references ["30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260507170000_graph_sos_intel.ts" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-graph-sos-intel/wire/manifest.jsonld" "90-docs/adr/2605071700-graph-sos-intel-actor.md"]} :blockchain-head-ingest-vke-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "operations" :severity "info" :status "removed" :summary "Bitcoin/Ethereum Vultr VKE head ingest was removed; history seed moves to BigQuery" :details "The Vultr VKE `blockchain` namespace was retired on 2026-05-09. Bitcoin and\nEthereum public-chain history ingest should seed from BigQuery public datasets;\nany future full node or chain-specific runtime belongs in a separate cluster,\nnot the Kotoba/Datomic-oriented Vultr VKE member cluster.\n\nKotoba/Datomic CREATE TABLE DDL for `vertex_blockchain_block` and\n`vertex_blockchain_tx` was cancelled by RW scheduler during the 2026-04-25\nincident window. Until RW DDL stabilizes, the worker lands deterministic block\nand tx rows into existing `vertex_blockchain_actor` with `props.kind` =\n`block|tx`; later backfill can project these rows into dedicated tables.\n" :impact "blockchain domain coverage, ingest cursor semantics, BigQuery seed planning, VKE cleanup" :related_files ["40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/ingest/blockchain.py" "90-docs/adr/2604251935-blockchain-vke-head-ingest.md"]} :global-product-resident-ingest-20260509 {:discovered_on "2026-05-09" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Global product ingest is evidence-first and runs through resident LangGraph, with official-site webfetch, intel, inference, GTIN identity, and kakaku offers" :details "ADR-2605091200 defines the Google-Shopping-like product graph as an internal\nproduct intelligence substrate, not as a Google Shopping scraper.\n\nPhase 1 schema is Alembic-owned under `alembic/current_versions`:\n- `vertex_product_source_page` records official/merchant page evidence,\n  fetch method, content hash, source kind, and authority rank.\n- `vertex_product_fact_evidence` records extracted product facts with\n  field-level source, method, confidence, model, and prompt version.\n- `vertex_product_ingest_frontier` stores the resident ingest backlog for\n  product hints, official URLs, merchant URLs, GTINs, retry state, and leases.\n- `vertex_product_ingest_run` records resident dispatcher runs and child\n  `global_product_enrich_one` dispatch responses.\n- `edge_product_official_source` links canonical product DIDs to official\n  manufacturer/brand pages.\n- `edge_product_brand_owner` links product/brand evidence to legal/entity\n  ownership candidates.\n\nRuntime assistant:\n- `global_product_enrich_one` is seeded as a `py_factory` LangGraph assistant\n  and deployed at `langgraph.builtin.global_product_enrich_one`.\n- It is the per-product transaction graph for official-page webfetch, merchant\n  webfetch, product fact extraction, brand-owner candidate resolution,\n  inference-backed match confidence, GTIN registration, kakaku offer ingest,\n  evidence writes, and audit.\n- `global_product_ingest_resident` is seeded as a `py_factory` LangGraph\n  assistant and deployed at `langgraph.builtin.global_product_ingest_resident`.\n  It selects bounded frontier batches, dispatches `global_product_enrich_one`\n  through LangGraph Server, updates retry/lease state, and writes run lineage.\n- `50-infra/vultr/mitama-langgraph-pool/templates/global-product-ingest-resident.yaml`\n  runs the resident trigger in `{{ .Values.namespace }}` and never creates\n  Kubernetes resources in the default namespace.\n\n`gtin.etzhayyim.com` continues to own canonical product identity. `kakaku.etzhayyim.com`\ncontinues to own merchant offers and price history. `yoro.etzhayyim.com` owns\noperator-facing product research summaries.\n" :impact "global product identity, price comparison, evidence lineage, LangGraph resident ingest" :related_files ["90-docs/adr/2605091200-global-product-resident-ingest-langgraph.md" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260509230000_global_product_ingest_evidence.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260509233000_global_product_ingest_resident.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/sql_migrations/20260509230000_global_product_ingest_evidence.up.sql" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/langgraph_graphs/global_product_enrich_one.py" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/langgraph_graphs/global_product_ingest_resident.py" "50-infra/vultr/mitama-langgraph-pool/templates/global-product-ingest-resident.yaml"]} :jp-fiscal-kysely-kotoba-coverage-20260427 {:discovered_on "2026-04-27" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "JP fiscal ingest uses Kysely/Kotoba/Datomic vertex_, edge_, mv_ schema; SQLite is not a valid persistence target" :details "ADR-0035 is implemented through Kysely migrations under\n30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/*jp_fiscal*.ts, with generated types in\n30-graph/graph-schema/src/database.ts. Source manifests live in\n60-apps/etzhayyim-project-states/data/jp_fiscal/sources.json, but they are not\nthe persistence SSoT.\n\nLive pipeline implemented 2026-04-27:\n- vertex_jp_fiscal_source / vertex_jp_fiscal_document\n- vertex_jp_fiscal_budget_book / vertex_jp_fiscal_appropriation\n- vertex_jp_fiscal_procurement_bid\n- edge_jp_fiscal_evidence / edge_jp_fiscal_flow\n- mv_jp_fiscal_* coverage for source-document, record-document, budget pipeline,\n  and procurement bid→contract gaps.\n\nOperational invariant:\n- DATABASE_URL is read from Apple Keychain service etzhayyim.rw account ROOT_URL.\n- Do not print the URL.\n- Do not use ON CONFLICT against Kotoba/Datomic; use DELETE+INSERT or explicit\n  SELECT-then-INSERT.\n- If Kysely migrator is blocked by historical out-of-band rows, use\n  scripts/apply-pending.sh for the exact migration, then run db:gen and db:drift.\n" :impact "JP fiscal graph schema, government money-flow ingest, procurement coverage" :references ["90-docs/adr/0035-jp-tax-money-flow-reverse-topology.md" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260427070000_jp_fiscal_graph.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260427100000_jp_fiscal_document_coverage.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260427131000_jp_fiscal_record_coverage.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260427133000_jp_fiscal_procurement_record_coverage.ts" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260427134500_jp_fiscal_procurement_pipeline_coverage.ts"]} :erc725-root-vector-search-20260427 {:discovered_on "2026-04-27" :category "identity-search" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Actor vector embeddings use ERC725 root DID; AT DIDs are facade/display keys" :details "ADR-0074 and ADR-2604262100 make `did:erc725:etzhayyim:260425:<identity>` the\ncanonical actor root. Actor semantic search and vector backfill therefore key\n`vertex_vector_embedding_source.source_uri` as\n`actor:did:erc725:etzhayyim:260425:<identity>`.\n\n`did:web` and `did:plc` are AT Protocol facade/profile keys only. They may be\nstored in `repo` for display/profile enrichment, but production actor HNSW\nsearch excludes legacy facade-keyed rows.\n\nYoro live root/facade pair:\n- root: `did:erc725:etzhayyim:260425:0xe506d815690ab0b81bf2f34b5057d7b8b96fe643`\n- facade: `did:web:yoro.etzhayyim.com`\n" :impact "view_actor_unified root_did projection, vector embedding source keys, AppView actor HNSW search" :related_files ["30-graph/graph-schema/scripts/migrate-rw-erc725-root.mjs" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/vector_embedding.py" "50-infra/cloudflare/workers/appview/src/appview/search.ts" "90-docs/adr/0074-ethereum-identity-bridge-cacao-webauthn.md" "90-docs/adr/2604262100-erc725-erc8004-k8s-ipfs-agent-runtime.md" "90-docs/adr/2604270015-vector-embedding-backfill-zeebe-worker.md"]} :flight-offer-price-spine-20260416 {:discovered_on "2026-04-16" :category "schema" :severity "info" :status "resolved" :summary "Flight pricing moved to dedicated graph table + cheapest-offer MV" :details "Follow-up to flight_graph_spine:\n- migration: 20260416110000_vertex_flight_offer.ts\n- table: vertex_flight_offer (offer_id/provider/route/date/price/currency/booking_url/deeplink_url)\n- MV: mv_flight_offer_cheapest_by_route_date\nThis avoids overloading generic vertex_spatial/vertex_other for fare listings and\nprovides a stable SQL path for route/date cheapest queries.\n" :impact "maps flight crawler/list API, fare ranking queries, booking link projection"}} :erc725_projection {:status "active" :script "30-graph/graph-schema/scripts/migrate-rw-erc725-root.mjs" :rw_url_env "KOTOBA_URL or DATABASE_URL" :rpc_url_env "ETH_PRIVATE_RPC_URL" :registry_addr_env "etzhayyim_ROOT_IDENTITY_REGISTRY_ADDR" :root_hash_rule "root_did_hash = keccak256(utf8(rootDid)) derived from resolved ERC725 identity address" :facade_rule "facade_did is lookup/display/federation input only" :verified_on "2026-04-27" :verified_counts {:view_root_erc725 1 :edge_actual_yoro 1 :embedding_erc725_actor 1}} :vector_search_768 {:status